  "id": "self-awareness-theory",
  "term": "self-awareness theory",
  "definition": "In this source, self-awareness theory refers to the idea that after personal failure, people who are strongly self-focused may feel intense distress and turn to immediately rewarding behaviors such as drinking to escape the self-relevance of those emotions. It frames such behavior as a maladaptive way of regulating emotion.",
